# .draugr.conf - Draugr settings for this project. Commit this file.
#
# It is shell, and Draugr sources it, which means running it. Draugr therefore
# records its hash the first time you accept it and refuses to source a version
# it has not seen before. After editing, run:  dr-trust
#
# Put anything personal in .draugr.local.conf instead (gitignored, sourced after
# this file, so it wins).

# The agent this project expects. Changing it later means dr-up --recreate: sbx
# freezes the agent into the sandbox spec when the mound is built.
#DRAUGR_AGENT=claude

# Arguments for the agent, in the agent's own spelling - "--continue" for Claude
# Code, "resume --last" for Codex. Set this here only if the PROJECT needs them;
# a habit like resuming by default is yours rather than the repo's, so it belongs
# in ~/.config/draugr/config (or .draugr.local.conf) instead of a committed file.
#DRAUGR_AGENT_ARGS=

# Network rules and setup commands live in the kit, not here:
#   .draugr/kit/spec.yaml
# See https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/kits/
#DRAUGR_KIT=.draugr/kit

# Ports this project's dev server needs.
#DRAUGR_PORTS="5173:5173"

# A service on your own machine the agent may call - a local Ollama, say. Bare
# port numbers; the address is worked out at every dr-up.
#DRAUGR_HOST_PORTS="11434"

# Run the AGENT itself on a model you host, rather than on its vendor's cloud.
# Commit this only if the PROJECT requires it: code that cannot leave the
# building is a property of the repository, but the model NAME is a property of
# whoever's machine is running it, and a teammate who has not pulled that model
# gets a failure at their first prompt. A preference rather than a requirement
# belongs in .draugr.local.conf.
#DRAUGR_MODEL="qwen3.8:27b"

# Where that model is served. A bare port must ALSO be in DRAUGR_HOST_PORTS
# above, and dr-go refuses to start when it is not. Note 11435 rather than the
# 11434 in the example above: that is the query-only proxy in
# share/ollama-proxy, and 11434 serves DELETE /api/delete as well as inference.
#DRAUGR_MODEL_URL="11435"

# Extra environment for the agent, as space-separated NAME=value pairs. Commit
# this only for something the PROJECT needs; a limit that follows your GPU
# rather than the repository belongs in .draugr.local.conf.
#DRAUGR_ENV="CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_1M_CONTEXT=1"

# Reference material the agent should be able to read but never change.
#DRAUGR_MOUNTS="/mnt/c/Docs/api:ro"

# Data files that are worked on but not committed until they are valid.
# These are exempt from the clean-tree check.
#DRAUGR_DATA="tmp/** *.parquet"
#DRAUGR_DATA_PUSH=auto
#DRAUGR_DATA_PULL=manual
